{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n`GerritClient.clone_change_ref` (src/rebar/review_bot/gerrit_client.py) builds a fetch URL whose userinfo part holds the bot user and `gerrit_bot_token` and passes it as a positional argument to `git fetch -q --depth 2`. The secret is therefore in the git process's command line for the length of the fetch. On 2026-11-22 at 19:32 PST a read-only `ps` sample on the prod host (taken for ultrashort-emaciated-krill) showed the full URL, password included, in the review-bot's git child. Anyone who can list processes on the host or in the container (`ps`, `/proc/<pid>/cmdline`, SSM command output, monitoring agents) can read it. The token is the review-bot account's dual-scope Gerrit credential (REST and git).\n\n## Approach\nRoot cause: `clone_change_ref` (src/rebar/review_bot/gerrit_client.py:347-360) percent-encodes `bot_user:gerrit_bot_token` into the fetch URL's userinfo and passes that URL as a positional git argument, so the kernel exposes it in the process's command line for the whole fetch.\n\nFix the class by moving every credential that reaches a git or curl child out of argv and into a channel only the process owner (and root) can read:\n\n1. **Review-bot fetch (Python).** Build the fetch URL with no userinfo (`<gerrit_base_url>/a/<project>`). Pass the bot's existing Basic auth value (`GerritClient._auth`, gerrit_client.py:74-76, already used for REST) to git as URL-scoped config `http.<gerrit_base_url>/.extraHeader = Authorization: Basic …`, supplied through git's own `GIT_CONFIG_COUNT` / `GIT_CONFIG_KEY_<n>` / `GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_<n>` environment variables, appended AFTER any inherited entries (the review-bot container already sets `GIT_CONFIG_COUNT=1` for `safe.directory`, infra/compose/docker-compose.yml:88-90, so overwriting index 0 would break the tickets clone). Set `GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0` for that child so a rejected header fails fast instead of prompting. Only the Gerrit fetch child gets this environment; the GitHub tickets fetch keeps the inherited environment, and the URL scoping means git would not send the header to any other host even if it did. Verified locally on git 2.56: `git config --get-urlmatch http.extraheader` returns the value for `https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/a/rebar` and nothing for `https://github.com/navapbc/rebar`. The review-bot image is `python:3.12-slim` (Dockerfile.reviewbot:5, Debian git 2.39), which supports `GIT_CONFIG_COUNT` (git >= 2.31). Keep `_redact` on error paths.\n2. **Operator infra scripts (bash)** that put a password in argv today: infra/gerrit/smoke-check.sh (curl `-u user:token`, `git clone https://user:token@…`), infra/gerrit/reviewbot-e2e.sh (curl `-u`, curl URL with `user:token@`), infra/gerrit/feature-branch-e2e.sh (curl `-u` in api_* helpers and the hook download), infra/gerrit/feature-branch-e2e-scenarios.sh (curl `-u`, `git push https://user:pw@…`), infra/gerrit/feature-branch-inventory.sh (curl `-u`), and .github/workflows/external-integration.yml:783,787 (curl `-u user:jira_token`). curl reads the `user = \"u:p\"` line from a config file given as `-K <(printf …)` (printf is a bash builtin, so the secret never reaches an argv, and process substitution is a pipe, so nothing touches disk); git gets the same `GIT_CONFIG_*` extraHeader environment as the Python fix, with the base64 produced by piping into `base64`.\n\nNo rebar config key, `REBAR_*` env var, or flag is added; `GIT_CONFIG_*`/`GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT` are git's own variables (the mechanism-delta ratchet only censuses `REBAR_*` env vars, scripts/_mechanism_delta/detect_config.py:83-95).\n\nNo rotation is performed by this change: the `[non-codebase]` rotation criterion is the operator's decision after the fix deploys and is verified on the box.\n\n## Scope\n- src/rebar/review_bot/gerrit_client.py — `clone_change_ref` URL without userinfo; Gerrit fetch child gets the URL-scoped auth header through `GIT_CONFIG_*` env.\n- tests/unit/test_review_bot_git_credential_argv.py (new) — guard tests.\n- tests/unit/test_git_timeout_bounds_77e1.py — keep its timeout/redaction tests consistent with the new URL shape if they assert on it.\n- infra/gerrit/smoke-check.sh, infra/gerrit/reviewbot-e2e.sh, infra/gerrit/feature-branch-e2e.sh, infra/gerrit/feature-branch-e2e-scenarios.sh, infra/gerrit/feature-branch-inventory.sh — credentials out of argv.\n- .github/workflows/external-integration.yml — Jira cleanup curl reads its credential from `-K`.\n- tests/scripts/test_feature_branch_inventory.py — assert the stub `curl`/`git` argv never carries the password.\n\n## Testing\n- Unit (new file): drive `clone_change_ref` with a fake `subprocess.run` that records argv and env; assert no argv element of any call contains the raw token, the percent-encoded token, or the base64 `user:token`; assert the Gerrit fetch child's env carries `http.<base>/.extraHeader` with the Basic value appended after an inherited `GIT_CONFIG_COUNT=1` entry (which stays intact) and `GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0`; assert the GitHub tickets fetch child's env carries no Authorization header. Edge: no inherited `GIT_CONFIG_COUNT` (index 0); non-numeric inherited count falls back without crashing.\n- Unit (same file, static guard over the class): scan infra/**/*.sh and .github/workflows/*.yml for `curl … -u \"<x>:$…\"`, `--user \"<x>:$…\"`, and `://<x>:$…@` URL userinfo; fail with the file:line of any hit.\n- Script test: tests/scripts/test_feature_branch_inventory.py additionally asserts the stub-recorded curl/git argv lines never contain the password the stub credential helper returned.\n- Real path, locally: run `clone_change_ref` against the live Gerrit with the machine's Gerrit credential (obtained with `git credential fill`, never printed) and confirm it fetches a real change ref; while it runs, sample `ps` and count (`grep -c`) occurrences of the credential, expecting 0, without printing command lines.\n- On the box after merge + autodeploy: during a real review, a read-only SSM `ps` sample filtered to counts only (`grep -c '@rebar.solutions'` on the review-bot's git children = 0), never printing command lines.\n- `make verify` green; `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` exits 0.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] No review-bot git invocation carries a credential in its argv; the fetch authenticates through a channel that is not in the command line (credential helper, or a header passed through the environment).\n- [ ] A test fails if `clone_change_ref` puts the bot token in the git argv.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] The review-bot Gerrit token is rotated after the fix deploys, since it has appeared in process listings."}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1795412376289507001,"uuid":"7dab1145-9937-4289-a839-d7c58c053422"}